B.BJ=new A.ft("Mary Queen of Scots",B.cI,"assets/images/cards/card_mary.png","The Queen who granted Greyfriars Kirkyard to Edinburgh in 1562...","Mary Stuart granted the gardens of the Franciscan convent to the town council in 1562 for use as a burial ground because St Giles kirkyard had become overcrowded.")
B.BP=new A.ft("Greyfriars Bobby",B.cI,"assets/images/cards/card_bobby.png","Not every story at Greyfriars is a dark one...","The legendary Skye Terrier who spent 14 years guarding the grave of his owner, John Gray, until his own death in 1872.")
B.BK=new A.ft("King Charles I",B.cI,"assets/images/cards/card_charles.png","A King whose religious policies ignited rebellion across Scotland...","King of England, Scotland, and Ireland whose attempts to impose the Anglican Book of Common Prayer on Presbyterian Scotland sparked the National Covenant of 1638.")
B.BO=new A.ft("William Burke",B.cI,"assets/images/cards/card_burke.png","One half of Edinburgh's most infamous murderous duo...","Irish immigrant who, along with William Hare, murdered at least 16 people in 1828 to sell their corpses to Dr Robert Knox for anatomical dissection. Hanged in 1829.")
B.BN=new A.ft("William Hare",B.cI,"assets/images/cards/card_hare.png","The partner who turned King's evidence to save his own neck...","Partner in crime to William Burke. Offered immunity from prosecution in exchange for testifying against Burke. Released from prison and fled Scotland.")
B.BH=new A.ft("Margaret Docherty",B.io,"assets/images/cards/card_margaret.png","You've uncovered Burke & Hare's downfall...","The final victim of Burke and Hare, also known as Madgy McGonegal. Her murder on Halloween 1828 led to their discovery and arrest.")
B.BM=new A.ft('George "Bluidy" McKenzie',B.io,"assets/images/cards/card_mckenzie.png","The ruthless Lord Advocate who earned his terrifying nickname...",'Sir George Mackenzie of Rosehaugh, Lord Advocate under Charles II, known as "Bluidy Mackenzie" for his brutal prosecution of the Covenanters.')
B.BI=new A.ft("Henrietta Maria",B.m8,"assets/images/cards/card_henrietta.png","Behind every king, a queen who changed history...","Queen consort of England, Scotland, and Ireland as the wife of King Charles I. Her Roman Catholic faith and influence on the court fueled Scottish Presbyterian suspicion.")
B.BL=new A.ft("The McKenzie Poltergeist",B.ip,"assets/images/cards/card_poltergeist.png","You've mastered every detail of Greyfriars Kirkyard...","One of the world's most documented poltergeist phenomena, said to dwell in the Black Mausoleum and the Covenanters' Prison after being disturbed in 1999.")
B.BQ=new A.ft("Dr Robert Knox",B.ip,"assets/images/cards/card_knox.png","You've traced the bodies back to their buyer...","Prominent Scottish anatomist and lecturer at Surgeon's Square who purchased the murdered victims of Burke and Hare for anatomical research.")
